  "text": "Recipe: Moong Dal Pakodi | Papdi Chaat\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Chaat\nIngredients: yellow moong daal, water, asafetida (hing), ENO, whole wheat flour, plant based yogurt (soy yogurt), boiled potatoes, kala chana (brown chickpeas), Green Chutney, Amla Chutney, Sonth (Sweet Tamarind Chutney), roasted cumin powder, freshly ground black pepper, banana, raisins, pomegranate\nCooking methods: no-cook, blend, boil, roast\nInstructions: MOONG DAL PAKODI: Soak 1/2 cup yellow moong daal in water for 4 hours. Drain the water, then grind with 1 to 2 tsp water and 1/4 tsp asafetida (hing). Add 1 tsp ENO and 1 tsp water. Mix well to form a batter. Transfer the batter into idli moulds. Steam for ten minutes. Then soak them in regular water (at room temperature) for 10 minutes.\nPAPDI: Make a tight dough with whole wheat flour and water. Made a large-sized roti. Using a cookie cutter or the top of a small bottle, make small-sized thin rotis. Cook them on low flame so that they become crispy.\nCHAAT: Assemble a plate with MOONG DAL PAKODI, some plant based yogurt (soy yogurt, for example), PAPDI, boiled potatoes, boiled kala chana (brown chickpeas), Green Chutney, Amla Chutney, & Sonth (Sweet Tamarind Chutney) Sprinkle some roasted cumin powder, freshly ground black pepper. Optionally add minced banana, raisins and pomegranate.\nNotes: This is a Whole Food Plant-Based recipe. Sub-recipes mentioned are Green Chutney, Amla Chutney, and Sonth (Sweet Tamarind Chutney). ENO is used as an ingredient.",
